## BUAT RINGKASAN

Architecture: Monolithic Layer 1 with Parallel EVM Execution, MonadBFT Consensus, MonadDb Storage
Core Components: MonadBFT, Asynchronous Execution Engine, MonadDb, P2P Networking, JSON-RPC, Block Explorer, Developer Tooling
Audit Count: 0 (no public audits published)
Major Upgrade Count: 1 (Testnet Launch "Monad Madness" 2025-02-19)

## Open Threads

- Audit status: No public audit reports for MonadBFT, Asynchronous Execution Engine, or MonadDb; auditor selection and timeline not announced
- Formal verification: No published formal verification of MonadBFT consensus safety/liveness proofs
- Validator economics: Staking parameters, slashing conditions, delegation mechanics, and reward curves not yet published
- Parallel execution benchmarks: Real-world conflict rates and throughput under DeFi workloads (Uniswap-style, lending, etc.) not publicly benchmarked
- State growth: Long-term state size projections and storage cost models for 10k TPS sustained load not published
- Client diversity: Only one client implementation (Rust) known; no second client team announced
- Upgrade mechanism: On-chain governance / hard fork coordination process for protocol upgrades not documented
- Cryptographic dependencies: Specific BLS signature library and curve (BLS12-381?) for MonadBFT not explicitly documented
- P2P protocol spec: Wire protocol specification not published separately from codebase
- Gas scheduling: Exact gas cost adjustments for parallel execution vs standard EVM not fully documented
- Precompile roadmap: Whether Monad will add custom precompiles beyond Ethereum set not confirmed
- Light client: Light client / verify sync protocol not documented
- Snapshot/sync: State sync / snapshot mechanism for fast node bootstrap not detailed
- MEV protection: No documented MEV mitigation (PBS, encrypted mempool, etc.) in current design
- Cross-chain: Native bridge / cross-chain messaging design not published